<title>ROMANIA: Romania to get $75 mln EBRD loan for water works.</title>
<headline>Romania to get $75 mln EBRD loan for water works.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania will receive a $75 million loan  from the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) to  upgrade water utilities, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>A ministry statement said the loan accord, to finance water works  in 10 Romanian cities, would be signed next Monday.</p>
<p>The EBRD had already committed $310 million for Romania's infrastructure  this year.</p>
<p>Last week, the EBRD announced plans to invest around $100 million  to support the privatisation of Romania's Romtelecom telephone utility.  That money could be formally approved in September.</p>
<p>The EBRD portfolio for Romania was $1.05 billion in January, with  around 60 percent of it allocated to support projects in the public  sector.</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
